    "title": "Cooler weather is here… for now - NewsBreak",
    "text": "COLUMBUS, Ga. (WRBL)- This afternoon we are tracking isolated storms moving through the region. This has helped cool our readings a good bit. Thursday: Temperatures will remain cooler for the end of the week. Highs will sit in the lower 90s tomorrow. Another wave of scattered storms is in store tomorrow. Winds will be a bit breezy at times, gusting up to 20 mph. Weekend: Rain chances will begin to decrease at the end of the week as high pressure returns to the forecast. This high will unfortunately, lead to another round of heat. Highs will jump to near 100 degrees Sunday. Heat Index temps will sit near 105 degrees. Next Week: The new heat dome will grow even stronger next week. Expect many areas to hit 100 on Monday and Tuesday. Heat Index readings will be near 110 for multiple days. Isolated showers and storms will finally return to the forecast by midweek. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WRBL.",
